.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt BUSYBOX-FINDUTILS 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm busybox-findutils ,
.Nm egrep ,
.Nm fgrep ,
.Nm find ,
.Nm grep ,
.Nm xargs
.Nd BusyBox file search and argument utilities
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm egrep
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Brq Ar PATTERN | Fl e Ar PATTERN ... | Fl f Ar FILE ...
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm fgrep
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Brq Ar PATTERN | Fl e Ar PATTERN ... | Fl f Ar FILE ...
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm find
.Op Fl HL
.Op Ar PATH
.Ar ...
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Op Ar ACTIONS
.Nm grep
.Op Fl HhnlLoqvsrRiwFE
.Op Fl m Ar N
.Op Fl A | Fl B | Fl C Ar N
.Brq Ar PATTERN | Fl e Ar PATTERN ... | Fl f Ar FILE ...
.Op Ar FILE
.Ar ...
.Nm xargs
.Op Ar OPTIONS
.Op Ar PROG ARGS
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These are the findutils applets of BusyBox 1.36.1 as built for Rach2.
.Bl -tag -width xargs
.It Nm egrep
Run
.Nm grep
with extended regular expressions, as with
.Fl E .
.It Nm fgrep
Run
.Nm grep
with literal patterns, as with
.Fl F .
.It Nm find
Search for files and perform actions on them.
The default path is the current directory; the default action is
.Fl print .
Actions are combined as described below.
.It Nm grep
Search files, or standard input, for a pattern.
.It Nm xargs
Run
.Ar PROG
on items read from standard input.
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Ss find traversal
.Bl -tag -width "-maxdepth N"
.It Fl L , Fl follow
Follow symbolic links.
.It Fl H
Follow only symbolic links given on the command line.
.It Fl xdev
Do not descend into directories on other file systems.
.It Fl maxdepth Ar N
Descend at most this many levels.
Zero applies actions only to command line arguments.
.It Fl mindepth Ar N
Do not act on the first
.Ar N
levels.
.It Fl depth
Act on a directory after traversing its contents.
.El
.Ss find actions
Adjacent actions are joined by an implicit
.Fl a .
With
.Fl a ,
a failed action stops evaluation of that conjunction for the current file;
with
.Fl o ,
a successful action stops evaluation of that disjunction.
The
.Fl a
operator has higher precedence than
.Fl o .
Parentheses group actions, and
.Ql \&!
inverts an action's success or failure.
.Bl -tag -width "-name PATTERN"
.It Fl name Ar PATTERN
Match the file name without its directory part.
.It Fl iname Ar PATTERN
Like
.Fl name ,
ignoring case.
.It Fl path Ar PATTERN
Match the path.
.It Fl ipath Ar PATTERN
Like
.Fl path ,
ignoring case.
.It Fl regex Ar PATTERN
Match the path against a regular expression.
.It Fl type Ar X
Match file type
.Ar X :
one of
.Ql f ,
.Ql d ,
.Ql l ,
.Ql b ,
.Ql c ,
.Ql s ,
or
.Ql p .
.It Fl executable
Match executable files.
.It Fl perm Ar MASK
Match exactly the specified mode bits.
A leading plus requires at least one mask bit; a leading minus requires
all mask bits.
.It Fl mtime Ar DAYS
Match a modification time exactly
.Ar N
days in the past, more than
.Ar N
with
.Ar +N ,
or less than
.Ar N
with
.Ar -N .
.It Fl atime Ar DAYS
Apply the same day comparison to access time.
.It Fl ctime Ar DAYS
Apply the same day comparison to status change time.
.It Fl mmin Ar MINS
Compare modification time in minutes using the same
.Ar +N ,
.Ar -N ,
or
.Ar N
forms.
.It Fl amin Ar MINS
Compare access time in minutes.
.It Fl cmin Ar MINS
Compare status change time in minutes.
.It Fl newer Ar FILE
Match modification times later than that of
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl inum Ar N
Match an inode number.
.It Fl samefile Ar FILE
Match the same file as
.Ar FILE .
.It Fl user Ar NAME/ID
Match the given owner.
.It Fl group Ar NAME/ID
Match the given group.
.It Fl size Ar N Ns Op Cm bck
Match size
.Ar N .
The suffix c selects bytes, k selects kilobytes, and b selects 512-byte
units, the default.
A leading plus matches larger files; a leading minus matches smaller files.
.It Fl links Ar N
Match exactly this many links, more with
.Ar +N ,
or fewer with
.Ar -N .
.It Fl empty
Match empty files or directories.
.It Fl prune
Do not descend into the current directory.
.El
.Pp
If none of the following actions is specified,
.Fl print
is assumed:
.Bl -tag -width "-exec CMD ARG +"
.It Fl print
Print the file name.
.It Fl print0
Print the file name followed by a NUL byte.
.It Fl exec Ar CMD ARG Cm \&;
Run the command with each occurrence of
.Ql {}
replaced by the file name.
The action fails if the command returns a nonzero status.
.It Fl exec Ar CMD ARG Cm +
Run the command with
.Ql {}
replaced by a list of file names.
.It Fl delete
Delete the current file or directory.
This enables
.Fl depth .
.It Fl quit
Exit.
.El
.Ss grep, egrep, fgrep
.Bl -tag -width "-e PATTERN"
.It Fl H
Prefix output with the file name and a colon.
.It Fl h
Omit the file name prefix.
.It Fl n
Prefix output with the line number and a colon.
.It Fl l
Print only names of matching files.
.It Fl L
Print only names of files without a match.
.It Fl c
Print only the count of matching lines.
.It Fl o
Print only the matching part of a line.
.It Fl q
Suppress output; return 0 if a pattern is found, 1 otherwise.
.It Fl v
Select lines that do not match.
.It Fl s
Suppress open and read errors.
.It Fl r
Recurse into directories.
.It Fl R
Recurse into directories and follow symbolic links.
.It Fl i
Ignore case.
.It Fl w
Match whole words.
.It Fl x
Match whole lines.
.It Fl F
Treat patterns as literal strings.
.It Fl E
Use extended regular expressions.
.It Fl m Ar N
Match at most this many times per file.
.It Fl A Ar N
Print this many lines of trailing context.
.It Fl B Ar N
Print this many lines of leading context.
.It Fl C Ar N
Print this many lines of leading and trailing context.
.It Fl e Ar PATTERN
Specify a pattern to match.
.It Fl f Ar FILE
Read patterns from a file.
.El
.Ss xargs
.Bl -tag -width "-E STR, -e[STR]"
.It Fl 0
Read NUL-terminated items.
.It Fl a Ar FILE
Read items from a file instead of standard input.
.It Fl o
Reopen standard input as
.Pa /dev/tty .
.It Fl r
Do not run a command when input is empty.
.It Fl t
Print each command to standard error before executing it.
.It Fl p
Ask whether to run each command.
.It Fl E Ar STR , Fl e Ns Op Ar STR
Stop processing input at
.Ar STR .
.It Fl I Ar STR
Replace occurrences of
.Ar STR
in the command and arguments with the input line.
.It Fl n Ar N
Pass at most this many arguments to the command.
.It Fl s Ar N
Limit the command line to this many bytes.
.It Fl P Ar N
Run at most this many commands in parallel.
.It Fl x
Exit if the size limit is exceeded.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl find / -name passwd
